# Obsidian resolves a plugin's download from a GitHub release tagged IDENTICALLY
# to the version in manifest.json — `releases/download/0.9.9/main.js`, with no
# `v`. npm's default tag-version-prefix is `v`, so the documented release flow
# (`npm version x.y.z`) silently produced tags Obsidian cannot resolve, and
# every 0.9.x release was unreachable to the plugin browser.
tag-version-prefix=
